       <section anchor="interrupt-generation" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5.3">
         <name slugifiedName="name-interrupt-generation">Interrupt Generation</name>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-5.3-1">Using the OPNET tools, interrupts to the multicast routing processor
-node are generated in several ways.  One is the arrival of a
-multicast packet along a packet stream (at the multicast routing
-processor node) when the packet is received by the MAC node and
